 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Sealing",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The mated pair keeps water out to IPX7 (IEC 60529). The header has its seal ring fitted at the factory; the receptacle seals all of its wires with one silicone rubber plate. The assembly is suited to potting."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Contacts and retention",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The connector has a double-spring construction, a housing lance and an inner lock mechanism."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Wire-to-wire use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The receptacle housing and contact are shared with the JWPF wire-to-wire connectors."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The header is a top-entry type that stands vertically on a 1.6 mm board, its contact tails clinched (kinked) through the board. Mated with its receptacle, the pair stands (21.3) mm above the board."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board pattern",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Board patterns are viewed from the connector mounting side. Contact holes are φ1 ±0.05 and the locating peg hole φ1.1 +0.1/0; hole pitch is held to ±0.05 without accumulating beyond ±0.05. The hole sizes are reference values and depend on the board material and how the holes are made: a hard laminate such as glass-fabric board needs larger holes."
  }
 ],
